A||N||1||Monkeyman||Just one word...Speed Bleeders||||1||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||08-12-2000||01:35 AM||||OK.  So that's 3 words.  Sue me.  Anyway, I just found their site today.  <A HREF="http://www.speedbleeder.com" TARGET=_blank>www.speedbleeder.com</A> <BR>These are bleeder screws that have a one way check valve in them.  You loosen them slightly (just like you would with originals), then bleed the brakes (each one individually) all by yourself.  $6.50US/each.  They have them to fit the stock Fiero calipers and also for the GA/Beretta calipers.  They don't have any for the clutch/slave cylinder/whatever it is yet, but they said if someone were to send thiers in, it could be modified with the check valve.  Just thought someone might want to know.  I'll be ordering mine tomorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jonathan||08-13-2000||10:26 AM||||Thinking about those myself.  Summit Racing carries the same things.  2 for $9.99.  Slight savings.  I have not called, but they say that they can fit most applications.||||reg||12
